=== start ===
# checkpoint: start
Water is for paying folk, but talk is free. I am Hattie. Bucket down, ears open.
-> hub

= hub
# checkpoint: start.hub
+ [Heard any rumors?]
  Funny you ask. A scavenger came through a few days back, trying to sell a <b>Nose Army radio</b>. Said he pulled it off an Army wagon sitting dead in the hills north-east of here. When the Farmers asked him where, exactly, he filled his tank and left for Nose in a hurry.
  ~ note("wagonBowl")
  -> hub
+ [Seen any strangers come through?]
  Every day. Traders, couriers, folk with a tank of fuel and a story. The ones that worry me are the quiet ones who ask where the seed stores are.
  -> hub
+ [Any local legends?]
  You know Glass Flats, out east? There is an Old World tank out there that <shake>still runs</shake>. Rolls out at night with its lights off. My cousin saw it. Well. Heard it.
  ~ note("glassTank")
  -> hub
+ [What do you make of Nose?]
  Soldiers playing at a town. They eat our grain and send us orders back. Polite enough, mind you, whenever they want something.
  -> hub
+ [Why does every truck carry a gun now?]
  Pierce will not insure one without. The Granary arms its trucks. The Senate lets even tenants carry. And any welder can cut a mount from hull plate in a day.
  Ridge Wrecks does the finest, I hear. Otto Brann signs each one. A signed gun, think of that. Folk used to sign a loaf.
  -> hub
+ [What about the glass at the Glass Flats?]
  Pim Arslan, the lens cutter, says every ripple in it leans one way. Toward the Fallen Sun. My cousin says it points at heaven. He drinks.
  Sun or heaven, I will not stand on it at noon.
  ~ note("talkGlassLean")
  -> hub
+ [Is it true the Sunward take strangers?]
  They say a stranger goes into the crater with the Sunward and does not come out. I say people come out of the crater green at the edges and quiet.
  I have never followed one in. Water is for paying folk, not for asking.
  ~ note("talkSunwardTake")
  -> hub
+ [Goodbye.]
  -> END
